WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.582 --> 00:00:19.464
We arrived at a large house in Chiswick, and Holmes directed our cab to wait around the corner.

2
00:00:20.285 --> 00:00:23.487
The family must have gone to bed because the house was dark except for a light in the

3
00:00:23.507 --> 00:00:26.368
front hall, which shone a small circle of light on the doorstep.

4
00:00:27.269 --> 00:00:31.331
Holmes, Lestrade, and I crouched in the shadow of the fence that separated the grounds from the street.

5
00:00:31.351 --> 00:00:34.337
"We may be here for a while," whispered Holmes.

6
00:00:35.278 --> 00:00:38.520
But soon the garden gate swung open, and a dark figure rushed up the path.

7
00:00:39.441 --> 00:00:43.344
We heard him open a window and watched his progress through the house as he uncovered his lantern

8
00:00:43.404 --> 00:00:43.945
in each room.

9
00:00:43.965 --> 00:00:47.368
"Let's nab him as he climbs out the window," said Lestrade.

10
00:00:48.209 --> 00:00:52.152
Before we could move, the man came down the path, carrying something white under his arm.

11
00:00:53.533 --> 00:00:56.856
Turning his back to us, he laid the object on the doorstep and gave it a sharp tap.

12
00:00:57.777 --> 00:01:01.340
The man was so intent on his task that he never heard us sneaking up behind him.

13
00:01:02.292 --> 00:01:03.852
In an instant we had him in handcuffs.

14
00:01:03.873 --> 00:01:06.013
"It's the man in the photograph!"

15
00:01:06.353 --> 00:01:07.073
I said to Holmes.

16
00:01:07.814 --> 00:01:11.455
But he was squatting on the doorstep, examining what remained of the fifth bust of Napoleon.

17
00:01:12.315 --> 00:01:14.616
At this point the door opened, and the house's owner emerged.

18
00:01:14.636 --> 00:01:16.096
"Mr. Brown?"

19
00:01:16.436 --> 00:01:16.936
said Holmes.

20
00:01:16.956 --> 00:01:20.737
"Yes," said the man, "and you must be Sherlock Holmes.

21
00:01:21.598 --> 00:01:23.178
I got your letter and did exactly as you said.

22
00:01:24.018 --> 00:01:26.139
e locked all the bedroom doors and pretended we were asleep.

23
00:01:26.899 --> 00:01:28.279
Now won't you come in for some refreshment?"

24
00:01:28.299 --> 00:01:30.100
"No, I'm afraid it's late.

25
00:01:31.552 --> 00:01:34.473
We must escort this prisoner to the police station," said Holmes.

26
00:01:35.353 --> 00:01:37.294
I summoned the cab and the four of us climbed in.

27
00:01:38.054 --> 00:01:39.934
The prisoner said nothing during the entire ride.

28
00:01:40.795 --> 00:01:45.116
As we left Lestrade and his prisoner at Scotland Yard, Holmes said, "Come to Baker Street around six

29
00:01:45.136 --> 00:01:48.737
o'clock tomorrow, Lestrade, and I'll show you what a truly unusual crime this is."

30
00:01:49.717 --> 00:01:51.377
The three of us met again the next evening.

31
00:01:52.218 --> 00:01:56.679
Lestrade had not been able to get any information from the prisoner, but Inspector Hill, the expert on

32
00:01:56.699 --> 00:02:00.360
the Italian Quarter, had identified him as Beppo, last name unknown.

33
00:02:01.332 --> 00:02:04.733
Although Holmes did not say anything, he seemed to be excited about something.

34
00:02:05.054 --> 00:02:08.235
A moment later the doorbell rang and an elderly man appeared at our door.

35
00:02:08.255 --> 00:02:10.216
"Mr. Sandeford of Reading?"

36
00:02:10.556 --> 00:02:11.076
said Holmes.

37
00:02:12.617 --> 00:02:16.038
The man nodded and removed a bust of Napoleon from the shoulder bag he was carrying.

38
00:02:16.058 --> 00:02:20.440
"You wrote that you wanted to buy this for ten pounds," he said to Holmes.

39
00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:24.041
"I think you should know that my wife paid less than a pound for it."

40
00:02:24.922 --> 00:02:27.983
"That doesn't bother me; I am so eager to have this particular bust."

41
00:02:28.903 --> 00:02:29.663
Holmes handed Mr.

42
00:02:29.703 --> 00:02:30.804
Sandeford a piece of paper.

43
00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:32.441
"Please sign this.

44
00:02:33.382 --> 00:02:36.625
It simply says that you transfer every possible right you had in the bust to me.

45
00:02:37.445 --> 00:02:39.067
Now here is your money and I wish you good evening."

46
00:02:40.007 --> 00:02:43.210
When our visitor had departed, Holmes took a white cloth and laid it on the table.

47
00:02:44.151 --> 00:02:47.414
Then he placed the bust in the center of the cloth and struck it with his riding crop.

48
00:02:48.275 --> 00:02:51.057
The bust shattered and Holmes bent eagerly over the fragments.

49
00:02:52.498 --> 00:02:56.362
With a shout of triumph, he held up a fragment that contained a round, dark object.

50
00:02:56.382 --> 00:02:58.504
"Gentlemen!" he cried.

51
00:02:59.428 --> 00:03:03.831
"Let me introduce you to the black pearl of Italy—the most famous pearl in the world."

52
00:03:04.672 --> 00:03:07.874
Lestrade and I were silent for a moment and then we burst into applause.

53
00:03:08.795 --> 00:03:11.897
A flush of color sprang to Holmes' pale cheeks, and he bowed to us.

54
00:03:11.917 --> 00:03:18.181
"I have traced the pearl," said Holmes, "from the princess of Colonna's bedroom at the Dacre Hotel, where

55
00:03:18.201 --> 00:03:21.164
it disappeared, to this bust manufactured by Gelder and Company.

56
00:03:22.104 --> 00:03:26.587
You will remember, Lestrade, the sensation when the pearl vanished and the vain efforts of the London police

57
00:03:26.607 --> 00:03:27.168
to recover it.

58
00:03:28.044 --> 00:03:30.767
The police consulted me about the case, but I was unable to solve it."

59
00:03:31.668 --> 00:03:33.369
"Wasn't the princess' maid a suspect?"

60
00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:34.390
asked Lestrade.

61
00:03:34.410 --> 00:03:36.452
"Yes," said Holmes.

62
00:03:36.472 --> 00:03:41.717
"She was an Italian woman with a brother in London, but we failed to find anything suspicious about

63
00:03:41.757 --> 00:03:42.498
their activities."

64
00:03:43.519 --> 00:03:46.001
Holmes explained that the maid's name was Lucretia Venucci.

65
00:03:46.802 --> 00:03:51.847
When Holmes heard that the man killed on the journalist's doorstep was Pietro Venucci, he suspected that Pietro

66
00:03:51.887 --> 00:03:52.648
was the maid's brother.

67
00:03:53.556 --> 00:03:57.999
Looking through his old newspapers, Holmes was able to determine that the pearl was stolen two days before

68
00:03:58.060 --> 00:03:59.761
Beppo was arrested at Gelder and Company.

69
00:03:59.781 --> 00:04:02.563
"At the very time these busts were being made!"

70
00:04:02.923 --> 00:04:03.884
Holmes said triumphantly.

71
00:04:03.904 --> 00:04:06.866
"But how does Beppo tie into the theft of the pearl?"

72
00:04:07.226 --> 00:04:07.627
I asked.

73
00:04:07.647 --> 00:04:11.690
"Beppo may have stolen the pearl from Pietro Venucci," said Holmes.

74
00:04:12.671 --> 00:04:16.714
"Or he may have been working with Pietro, or he may have been the go-between for Pietro and

75
00:04:16.734 --> 00:04:17.614
his sister, Lucretia.

76
00:04:19.075 --> 00:04:19.676
It doesn't matter.

77
00:04:20.352 --> 00:04:24.015
What's important is that Beppo had the pearl when the police were pursuing him and he knew he

78
00:04:24.075 --> 00:04:24.656
had to hide it."

79
00:04:25.576 --> 00:04:27.878
Beppo had run into the sculpture factory where he worked.

80
00:04:28.739 --> 00:04:31.521
Six plaster casts of Napoleon were drying in the passage.

81
00:04:32.582 --> 00:04:33.683
One of them was still soft.

82
00:04:34.203 --> 00:04:38.327
In an instant Beppo made a small hole in the wet plaster, inserted the pearl, and covered the

83
00:04:38.367 --> 00:04:41.669
hole. "But Beppo went to prison for a year," I said.

84
00:04:41.689 --> 00:04:44.431
"How did he find the six busts when he was released?"

85
00:04:45.372 --> 00:04:49.716
Holmes explained that Beppo used a cousin employed at Gelder to learn which shops had bought the busts.

86
00:04:50.716 --> 00:04:54.418
Then Beppo managed to find employment with Morse Hudson and was able to track down three of the

87
00:04:54.458 --> 00:05:00.100
busts. When Beppo failed to find the pearl in any of the Morse Hudson busts, he investigated those

88
00:05:00.180 --> 00:05:01.300
sold by Harding Brothers.

89
00:05:02.801 --> 00:05:06.322
With the help of an Italian employee, he learned where those three busts had gone.

90
00:05:07.243 --> 00:05:11.104
He was followed to the journalist's house by Venucci, who blamed him for the loss of the pearl.

91
00:05:11.925 --> 00:05:14.826
In their ensuing scuffle, Beppo killed Venucci on the doorstep.

92
00:05:15.746 --> 00:05:20.328
"If the culprits knew each other," said Lestrade, "why was Venucci carrying Beppo's photograph?"

93
00:05:21.256 --> 00:05:24.197
"In case Venucci needed to ask anyone, 'Have you seen this man?'"

94
00:05:24.557 --> 00:05:25.097
said Holmes.

95
00:05:26.117 --> 00:05:29.158
After the journalist's bust was destroyed, there were only two left.

96
00:05:30.079 --> 00:05:33.940
Holmes decided that Beppo would try the one in Chiswick first because it was closer than Reading.

97
00:05:33.960 --> 00:05:37.681
"Last night I sent a letter by express messenger to warn Mr.

98
00:05:37.721 --> 00:05:39.301
Brown in Chiswick," said Holmes.

99
00:05:39.321 --> 00:05:43.842
"When we failed to find the pearl there, I knew it must be in the last bust, and

100
00:05:43.882 --> 00:05:44.302
here it is."

101
00:05:44.322 --> 00:05:46.363
"Well, Mr.

102
00:05:46.403 --> 00:05:49.564
Holmes," said Lestrade, "We're not jealous of you at Scotland Yard.

103
00:05:50.428 --> 00:05:53.951
No, sir, we're very proud of you, and if you come down tomorrow there's not a man who

104
00:05:53.971 --> 00:05:55.332
wouldn't be glad to shake your hand."

105
00:05:55.352 --> 00:05:56.813
"Thank you!"

106
00:05:57.153 --> 00:05:58.915
said Holmes, turning away from Lestrade.

107
00:05:59.815 --> 00:06:04.118
At Lestrade's words, the great detective seemed more affected by emotion than I'd ever seen him.

108
00:06:04.999 --> 00:06:07.981
But a moment later, he was the cold, practical thinker once again.

109
00:06:08.001 --> 00:06:10.283
"Good-bye, Lestrade," he said.

110
00:06:10.303 --> 00:06:15.027
"When any little problem comes your way, I'll be happy, if I can, to give you a hint

111
00:06:15.087 --> 00:06:16.528
or two about its solution."
